          <Rectangle Name="Rectangle2">
            <ReportItems>
              <Textbox Name="Textbox63">
                <CanGrow>true</CanGrow>
                <KeepTogether>true</KeepTogether>
                <Paragraphs>
                  <Paragraph>
                    <TextRuns>
                      <TextRun>
                        <Value>CONDITIONS OF PURCHASE, PAYMENT AND DOCUMENTATION :</Value>
                        <Style>
                          <FontFamily>Segoe UI</FontFamily>
                          <FontSize>9pt</FontSize>
                          <FontWeight>Bold</FontWeight>
                          <TextDecoration>Underline</TextDecoration>
                        </Style>
                      </TextRun>
                      <TextRun>
                        <Value xml:space="preserve">
</Value>
                        <Style>
                          <FontFamily>Segoe UI</FontFamily>
                          <FontSize>9pt</FontSize>
                          <TextDecoration>Underline</TextDecoration>
                        </Style>
                      </TextRun>
                      <TextRun>
                        <Value>

1.  Corrections on PO are not allowed unless validated by the person who has authorized the PO at the first instance</Value>
                        <Style>
                          <FontFamily>Segoe UI</FontFamily>
                          <FontSize>9pt</FontSize>
                        </Style>
                      </TextRun>
                    </TextRuns>
                    <Style />
                  </Paragraph>
                  <Paragraph>
                    <TextRuns>
                      <TextRun>
                        <Value>
2.  Original Delivery Note(s) signed by the recipient should be attached to the invoice (copies are not acceptable)</Value>
                        <Style>
                          <FontFamily>Segoe UI</FontFamily>
                          <FontSize>9pt</FontSize>
                        </Style>
                      </TextRun>
                    </TextRuns>
                    <Style />
                  </Paragraph>
                  <Paragraph>
                    <TextRuns>
                      <TextRun>
                        <Value>
3.  Multiple invoices for a single PO are not acceptable. Invoices are to be submitted to Accounts Department of GulfNet

4.  The PO number should be quoted on all correspondence. All Correspondence to be Addressed To :  Accounts GulfNet
     P.O. Box  44542</Value>
                        <Style>
                          <FontFamily>Segoe UI</FontFamily>
                          <FontSize>9pt</FontSize>
                        </Style>
                      </TextRun>
                    </TextRuns>
                    <Style />
                  </Paragraph>
                  <Paragraph>
                    <TextRuns>
                      <TextRun>
                        <Value>
5.  The quantity of goods supplied shall be as stated on the PO, unless otherwise agreed by GulfNet Accounts in writing  before hand. Any        unauthorized excess will be liable or rejection.

6.  The delivery date and place shall be as stated on the PO, unless otherwise agreed by GulfNet, Accounts in writing beforehand GulfNet has the right to reject goods not delivered at the place and date as specified in the PO unless otherwise agreed.

7.  Goods must be in accordance with specification stated on the PO. Goods of incorrect specifications or of inferior quality may be turned at the       supplier's risk and expense within 15 working days. Goods are considered accepted only after they have checked to be satisfactory by                   GulfNet and  not against signature on Delivery Notes.

8.  Original invoices alone will be considered for payment.

9.  All packages must be adequately packed for the mode of delivery. The supplier may be held responsible for any damage incurred  due to             bad or insufficient packing.

10.  Dispute arising in respect of the order are subject to jurisdiction of Courts in respective locations of GulfNet Offices, where the PO                 issued
		
</Value>
                        <Style>
                          <FontFamily>Segoe UI</FontFamily>
                          <FontSize>9pt</FontSize>
                        </Style>
                      </TextRun>
                      <TextRun>
                        <Value>For Overseas Suppliers :</Value>
                        <Style>
                          <FontFamily>Segoe UI</FontFamily>
                          <FontSize>9pt</FontSize>
                          <FontWeight>Bold</FontWeight>
                        </Style>
                      </TextRun>
                      <TextRun>
                        <Value>

1. Shipping invoices: Two certified copies of invoices are necessary. Certified invoices must state:</Value>
                        <Style>
                          <FontFamily>Segoe UI</FontFamily>
                          <FontSize>9pt</FontSize>
                        </Style>
                      </TextRun>
                    </TextRuns>
                    <Style />
                  </Paragraph>
                  <Paragraph>
                    <TextRuns>
                      <TextRun>
                        <Value>    a. We certify that these goods are of origin. </Value>
                        <Style>
                          <FontFamily>Segoe UI</FontFamily>
                          <FontSize>9pt</FontSize>
                        </Style>
                      </TextRun>
                    </TextRuns>
                    <Style>
                      <TextAlign>Left</TextAlign>
                    </Style>
                  </Paragraph>
                  <Paragraph>
                    <TextRuns>
                      <TextRun>
                        <Value>    b. GulfNet PO number.  
    c. Full description of goods, quantities and prices in accordance with the delivery terms. 
    d. Number of packages, net and gross weight in kilos and measurement in meters of each package against respective package numbers.</Value>
                        <Style>
                          <FontFamily>Segoe UI</FontFamily>
                          <FontSize>9pt</FontSize>
                        </Style>
                      </TextRun>
                    </TextRuns>
                    <Style />
                  </Paragraph>
                  <Paragraph>
                    <TextRuns>
                      <TextRun>
                        <Value>
2. Shipping documents: The following documents are required for Customs purposes:
    a. Two certified invoices as stated in (1) above.
    b. Two original and two copies of Bill of Lading (sea freight shipments only)
    c. One original Certificate of Origin plus one copy issued by a Chamber of Commerce or approved Trade Federation and 
         legalized by an official Arab Representative, Legation or Consulate in the exporting country.
    d. Airway Bill (airfreight shipments only)
    e. Packing list.</Value>
                        <Style>
                          <FontFamily>Segoe UI</FontFamily>
                          <FontSize>9pt</FontSize>
                        </Style>
                      </TextRun>
                    </TextRuns>
                    <Style />
                  </Paragraph>
                  <Paragraph>
                    <TextRuns>
                      <TextRun>
                        <Value xml:space="preserve">    </Value>
                        <Style>
                          <FontFamily>Segoe UI</FontFamily>
                        </Style>
                      </TextRun>
                      <TextRun>
                        <Value>f. Shipping marks to include GulfNet</Value>
                        <Style>
                          <FontFamily>Segoe UI</FontFamily>
                          <FontSize>9pt</FontSize>
                        </Style>
                      </TextRun>
                    </TextRuns>
                    <Style />
                  </Paragraph>
                  <Paragraph>
                    <TextRuns>
                      <TextRun>
                        <Value>
3.  The supplier may be held responsible for demurrage charges at Sea Port or Airport if the necessary documents are not Provided in due time         forclearance.</Value>
                        <Style>
                          <FontFamily>Segoe UI</FontFamily>
                          <FontSize>9pt</FontSize>
                        </Style>
                      </TextRun>
                    </TextRuns>
                    <Style />
                  </Paragraph>
                  <Paragraph>
                    <TextRuns>
                      <TextRun>
                        <Value>
4. Processing this PO implies acceptance of the terms and conditions mentioned above.</Value>
                        <Style>
                          <FontFamily>Segoe UI</FontFamily>
                          <FontSize>9pt</FontSize>
                        </Style>
                      </TextRun>
                    </TextRuns>
                    <Style />
                  </Paragraph>
                </Paragraphs>
